cases.instruction:
`aro check` reports:
```
  8:13: warning: Variable 'fallback' is defined but never used
```

```aro
(Application-Start: Config) {
    Extract the <raw> from the <env: LIMIT>.
    match <raw> {
        case /^[1-9][0-9]*$/ {
            Transform the <limit: int> from the <raw>.
        }
        case /^$/ {
            Create the <fallback> with 1000.
        }
    }
    Log <limit> to the <console>.
    Return an <OK: status> for the <startup>.
}
```

Fix the warning.

cases.output:
`<fallback>` is never read, but its binding is the ONLY statement in the `case /^$/` block — deleting the line alone would leave an empty block, which does not parse. Remove the whole case:

```aro
(Application-Start: Config) {
    Extract the <raw> from the <env: LIMIT>.
    match <raw> {
        case /^[1-9][0-9]*$/ {
            Transform the <limit: int> from the <raw>.
        }
    }
    Log <limit> to the <console>.
    Return an <OK: status> for the <startup>.
}
```

